# TypeScript Standards

- Use strict TypeScript. Avoid `any`; if unavoidable, justify in a short comment.
- Prefer explicit return types on exported functions and use cases.
- Validate untrusted input at the presentation/config boundary; keep domain types trusted.
- Use `unknown` for caught errors and narrow before use.
- Keep modules ESM-friendly and side-effect free except composition root / adapters.
